# proof-of-feature: FR2355 diag console bring-up

Durable, committed evidence that the diagnostic firmware **boots and its backchannel console works on
real FR2355 silicon** (per the `prove-firmware-on-hardware` skill). Volatile run header is kept
separate from the stable assertion body so a re-proof of unchanged behaviour diffs cleanly.

## Run header (volatile — regenerate on re-proof)
- feature .......... FR2355 diag console bring-up (backchannel UART)
- as-run build ..... fr2355/2026.dev-hd2355  (HEAD, post bsp-extraction + prod-convergence/union-i2c)
- observed ......... 2026-09-30  (re-proof at HEAD, single-adapter)
- target part ...... MSP430FR2355  (JTAG device-id 0x01ff)
- board / serial ... FR2355 LaunchPad, eZ-FET serial 8E57A36E1F000000  (@toy-b)
- console endpoint . /dev/cu.usbmodem235103  (9600 8N1)
- channels used .... flash byte-verify (mspdebug) + console verify-by-stamp + console log capture
- tool ............. `thepia hwd msp flash ... --verify-stamp hd2355`
- prior run ........ fr2355/2026.dev-fr2355run1 (2026-09-29, pre-refactor) — same result

## Assertions (stable — expected vs observed)
| # | assertion | expected | observed | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | firmware boots to the POST loop | repeating POST banner | banner + repeating POST captured | PASS |
| 2 | console UART transmits, correct baud | readable ASCII @9600 on UCA1/P4.3 | clean ASCII; exact stamp substring matched (a wrong baud can't match cleanly) | PASS |
| 3 | build identity echoed | flashed stamp on the banner | `build fr2355/2026.dev-fr2355run1` | PASS |
| 4 | clock/SMCLK = 1 MHz (FLL locked) | clean 9600 (garbled if unlocked) | clean console; corroborated by prior SBW read CSCTL7=0x0447 (FLL locked, SMCLK 1.015 MHz) | PASS |
| 5 | Leaf-I²C master runs a bus scan | scan executes and reports | `I2C scan: ...` runs each POST | PASS |

Overall: **PASS** — console bring-up proven on FR2355 silicon.

Note on #5: the FR2355 board's I²C bus reads stuck-low (`SDA=L SCL=L`, "105 UNEXPECTED", id-reads
FAILED) because no sensor shield / pull-ups are attached — a hardware-attach condition, NOT a firmware
fault. The assertion is that the Leaf-I²C master *runs*; device presence is out of scope here.

## Tool evidence (verbatim)
    programmed diag/target/msp430-none-elf/release/diag via msp-ezfet (part: MSP430FR2355 (id = 0x01ff))
      flash-verified (byte-compare) by mspdebug.
      CONFIRMED RUNNING: the board printed "fr2355run1".
        evidence: build fr2355/2026.dev-fr2355run1

