## Status / re-proof trigger
- **RE-PROOFED AT HEAD 2026-09-30 (single-adapter).** The pending trigger is satisfied: the current
  tree — after the `bsp` extraction (board/hal/i2c moved to crates/bsp) and the prod-convergence
  union `i2c` — runs on real FR2355 silicon. Two extra confirmations this run:
  - **board-aware UART dump** (`regs.rs` → `board::console_uart_regs`) prints `[console UART]
    UCAx CTLW0=0080 BRW=0006 MCTLW=2081` — reads **UCA1** correctly (pre-fix it dumped UCA0).
  - **union `i2c`** (`bsp::i2c`, diag `set_brw` + prod `bus_levels`/`read_reg_pumped`/probe) — the
    Leaf master inits (`UCB0CTLW0=0F80`, 100 kHz) and the scan executes; no regression vs the prior run.
- Not yet proven here (future): the SBW boot-record channel (`bootrec.rs` is dormant/unwired) and the
  Tier-2 SoM-mastered I²C/UART acceptance (full bench). This log is Tier-1 (dev-board) console proof.
